 3. Noto Sans, by the Noto Project Authors.
    Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors
    (https://github.com/notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic).
    SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 -- https://scripts.sil.org/OFL

    Redistributed as RASTERISED SIGNED-DISTANCE-FIELD GLYPHS in two places,
    both of them produced by Mapbox's `sdf-glyph-foundry` and served by
    OpenFreeMap rather than rasterised here:

      a. packages/frontend/scripts/mapgen/fixtures/fallback/ -- the code
         points Inter does not draw, for the six ranges GoWay completes
         locally, plus a manifest of what the upstream fallback serves. About
         78 kB. These are a build INPUT.

      b. packages/frontend/public/map/fonts/ -- the same glyphs, merged into
         GoWay's own Inter ranges and re-based onto Inter's ascender, in the
         six ranges listed as COMPLETED_RANGES in
         packages/frontend/scripts/build-map-glyphs.ts. These ARE served to
         browsers. A range GoWay cannot complete is not published at all and
         is proxied from OpenFreeMap at request time instead, so most of Noto
         reaches a user without passing through this repository.

    Plus ONE 76 kB glyph range (`Noto Sans Regular`, codepoints 0-255)
    committed at packages/frontend/scripts/mapgen/fixtures/ as a TEST FIXTURE.
    It is never served. It is the reference file against which GoWay's own
    glyph encoder is checked, and it is committed rather than fetched so that
    the check is offline and cannot pass because a third-party host was
    unreachable.

    The OFL permits this, and the permission was read off the font rather than
    off a web page. NotoSans-Regular.ttf, version 2.015, measured with fontkit:
    the `name` table's license record is "This Font Software is licensed under
    the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1"; it declares no Reserved Font Name,
    so the derived ranges may keep the name; and OS/2 fsType is
    {noEmbedding: false, viewOnly: false, editable: false, noSubsetting: false,
    bitmapOnly: false} -- installable embedding, with no restriction on
    subsetting or editing. The same file reports ascent 1069 at unitsPerEm
    1000, which is where the 26px ascender recorded in
    scripts/mapgen/fixtures/fallback/coverage.json comes from
    (ceil(1069 / 1000 * 24)); the glyphs' own metrics agree with it
    independently.

Map DATA is a separate obligation and is discharged separately: GoWay renders
OpenStreetMap-derived vector tiles served by OpenFreeMap in the OpenMapTiles
schema, and the resulting ODbL attribution travels with the style document
(`attribution` on its source) and is rendered in the product by
packages/frontend/components/map/MapAttribution.tsx. It is not vendored here.

